    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d810">

                <pb facs="0765" n="649" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg649"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/14325.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-01">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 1, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>General Benjamin Hill is in command of city during the absence of Obregon in Vera
                    Cruz. Zapatistas continue to occupy the farthest southern suburbs; they still
                    control and have cut the main city water supply. The Constitutionalists are
                    operating the Mexican Railway.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Silliman.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
